'''''Avengers: Doomsday''''' is an upcoming American [[superhero film]] based on the [[Marvel Comics]] superhero team the [[Avengers (comics)|Avengers]]. Produced by [[Marvel Studios]]<!-- and [[AGBO]], --> and distributed by [[Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures]], it is intended to be the sequel to ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]'' (2019) and [[List of Marvel Cinematic Universe films|the 39th film]] in the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] (MCU). Directed by [[Anthony and Joe Russo]], and written by [[Stephen McFeely]] and [[Michael Waldron]], the film features an [[ensemble cast]] led by [[Robert Downey Jr.]] as [[Victor von Doom (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Doctor Doom]].<!-- This formatting per talk page --> In the film, the [[Avengers (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Avengers]], [[Wakanda (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Wakandans]], [[New Avengers (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|New Avengers]], [[Fantastic Four (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Fantastic Four]], and the [[X-Men (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|X-Men]] converge from different universes to face Doom amidst the collapse of the [[Multiverse (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|multiverse]].<!-- Please do NOT add about Patrick Stewart's death here! -->

Two new ''Avengers'' films, ''The Kang Dynasty'' and ''[[Avengers: Secret Wars|Secret Wars]]'', were announced in July 2022 as the conclusion of the MCU's [[Marvel Cinematic Universe: Phase Six|Phase Six]] and "[[The Multiverse Saga]]". [[Jonathan Majors]] was set to reprise his MCU role as the villain [[Kang the Conqueror (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Kang the Conqueror]], with [[Destin Daniel Cretton]] and [[Jeff Loveness]] hired to direct and write ''The Kang Dynasty'', respectively. In November 2023, Cretton departed, Waldron replaced Loveness as writer, and Marvel was considering moving away from the Kang storyline, in part due to [[Jonathan Majors#Legal issues|Majors's legal issues]]; Majors was fired the following month. The return of the Russo brothers as directors and McFeely as co-writer, the casting of Downey as new villain Doctor Doom, and the new subtitle ''Doomsday'' were all announced in July 2024. The large cast features actors from previous MCU media and [[20th Century Fox]]'s [[X-Men (film series)|''X-Men'' film series]], using the idea of colliding universes to bring together actors from different franchises. Filming took place from April to September 2025 at [[Pinewood Studios]] in England, with location filming in England and Bahrain.<!-- Please do NOT add about Patrick Stewart's death here! -->

''Avengers: Doomsday'' will premiere at the [[Intuit Dome]] in Los Angeles on December 14, 2026, and is scheduled to be released in the United States on December 18, as part of Phase Six of the MCU. The sequel, ''Avengers: Secret Wars'', is set to be released on December 17, 2027.<!-- Please do NOT add about Patrick Stewart's death here! -->

== Premise ==
Fourteen months after the events of ''[[Thunderbolts*]]'' (2025),<ref name="ThunderboltsNewAvengers" /> amidst the collapse of the [[Multiverse (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|multiverse]], groups of heroes from three different universes—the [[Avengers (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Avengers]], [[Wakanda (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Wakandans]], and [[New Avengers (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|New Avengers]] from [[Earth-616 (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Earth-616]]; the [[Fantastic Four (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Fantastic Four]] from [[Earth-828]]; and the [[X-Men (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|X-Men]] from [[Earth-10005]]—converge to face the existential threat of [[Victor von Doom (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Doctor Doom]].<ref name="FeigeRussosCinemaConEW" /><ref name="FeigeCinemaConSR" /><ref name="EncoreScenesEW" />

== Cast ==
<!-- Order per https://www.marvel.com/movies/avengers-doomsday -->
* [[Robert Downey Jr.]] as [[Victor von Doom (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Victor von Doom / Doctor Doom]]:<br />A [[sorcerer (fantasy)|sorcerer]] and the ruler of the Eastern European country of [[Latveria (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Latveria]] who wields dark magic, following a tragic and personal loss.<ref name="DoomEmpireNov2026" /><ref name="DowneyDoomVoice" /><ref name="EWCoverStoryNov2026" /> He hails from [[Earth-828]], the same universe as the [[Fantastic Four (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Fantastic Four]]—a team with whom Doom has an established relationship, particularly with their leader Reed Richards. This connection reflects the long history these characters share in the comics, wherein Doom typically serves as the team's [[arch-nemesis]].<ref name="EWCoverStoryNov2026" /> Producer [[Kevin Feige]] said Doom was not an alternate universe "[[Variant (Marvel Cinematic Universe term)|variant]]" of Downey's previous [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] (MCU) character, the hero [[Tony Stark (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Tony Stark / Iron Man]].<ref name="DoomEmpireNov2026" /> Downey described Doom as a master manipulator and willing to go [[scorched earth]],<ref name="DowneyDoomManipulator" /><ref name="EWCoverStoryNov2026" /> and said he had a "glorious time" once he embraced being a villain, similar to how [[Michael Douglas]]'s character in the film ''[[Falling Down]]'' (1993) realizes that he is "the bad guy".<ref name="DowneyDoomVoice" /> Directors [[Anthony and Joe Russo]] said Doom was [[Gothic fiction|Gothic]] and more ego-driven than [[the Infinity Saga]]'s antagonist [[Thanos (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Thanos]], and "profoundly damaged" by the trauma of losing a child,<ref name="DoomEmpireNov2026" /> while Anthony Russo described him as "a wounded figure".<ref name="EWCoverStoryNov2026" /> Downey contributed costume ideas and developed his own backstory as reference for his performance.<ref name="DowneyBackstory" /> While initially hesitant about using an Eastern European accent, he found a voice that worked for the character while recording a manifesto speech he wrote.<ref name="DowneyDoomVoice" /> Because Doom wears a mask throughout the film, Downey focused on conveying emotions with his eyes.<ref name="DowneyMaskEyeActing" />
* [[Chris Evans (actor)|Chris Evans]] as [[Steve Rogers (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Steve Rogers<!-- Do NOT add Captain America as he has only been marketed as "Steve Rogers" -->]]:<br />The former leader of the [[Avengers (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Avengers]], a [[super soldier]], and [[World War II]] veteran who was the first person to carry the [[Captain America]] mantle. He returned to the 1940s at the end of the film ''[[Avengers: Endgame]]'' (2019) to live with Peggy Carter.<ref name="FirstTeaserRogersVariety" /> After that "definitive ending",<ref name="RogersTeaserOnlineTotalFilm" /> Evans said he would only return to the MCU if there was a good reason. He believed the story for ''Doomsday'' had a "very real reason that these heroes need Steve Rogers ‌now".<ref name="CinemaCon2026Reuters" /> Evans and Mackie indicated that Rogers would take on the [[Nomad (Marvel Comics)|Nomad]] mantle, similar to the comics.<ref name="EvansNomadJul2026" /><ref name="MackieNomadJul2026" />
* [[Chris Hemsworth]] as [[Thor (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Thor]]:<br />The [[Asgard (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Asgardian]] god of thunder and a founding Avenger, based on the [[Norse mythology|Norse mythological]] deity [[Thor]].<ref name="CastAnnouncementTHR" /> The character returns to the warrior-like persona and mindset last seen in the film ''[[Avengers: Infinity War]]'' (2018), with Joe Russo explaining that Thor seeks to "achieve meaning through battle".<ref name="RussosThorSep2026"/> Hemsworth said that Thor would feel "a strange hynoptic familiarity" while facing Doom, but would harbor uncertainty and mistrust towards him.<ref name="EWCoverStoryNov2026" />
* [[Pedro Pascal]] as [[Reed Richards (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Reed Richards / Mister Fantastic]]:<br />A highly intelligent scientist and the leader of the Fantastic Four on Earth-828, who can stretch any part of his body to great lengths.<ref name="SDCC2024F4" /> Pascal said Reed and Doom are "bonded in a lot of different ways", including as fellow scientists,<ref name="FeigeEmpireNov2026" /> while Joe Russo stated that the "love and respect that [they] have for each other in ''Doomsday'' is critical" to the film's story.<ref name="EWCoverStoryNov2026" />
* [[Paul Rudd]] as [[Scott Lang (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Scott Lang / Ant-Man]]: An Avenger and former petty criminal with [[Ant-Man suit (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|a suit]] that allows him to shrink or grow in scale while increasing in strength<ref name="CastAnnouncementTHR" />
* [[Anthony Mackie]] as [[Sam Wilson (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Sam Wilson / Captain America]]:<br />An Avenger and former [[pararescueman]] who was trained by the military in aerial combat using a specially designed wing pack,<ref name="Mackie" /> and who has assembled a new team of Avengers in ''Doomsday''<ref name="FeigeEmpireNov2026" />
* [[Florence Pugh]] as [[Yelena Belova (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Yelena Belova / Black Widow]]:<br />A member of the [[New Avengers (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|New Avengers]] who was trained in the [[Red Room (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Red Room]] as a [[Black Widows (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Black Widow]] assassin.<ref name="CastAnnouncementTHR" /> Feige said ''Doomsday'' would be "anchored" by Belova.<ref name="FeigePughAnchor" />
* [[Vanessa Kirby]] as [[Sue Storm (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Sue Storm / Invisible Woman]]:<br />Reed's wife and a member of the Fantastic Four on Earth-828 who can generate force fields and turn invisible.<ref name="SDCC2024F4" /> Joe Russo said Sue is "more cautious" regarding Doom than Reed is.<ref name="EWCoverStoryNov2026" />
* [[Ebon Moss-Bachrach]] as [[Ben Grimm (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Ben Grimm / The Thing]]:<br />Reed's best friend and a member of the Fantastic Four on Earth-828 whose skin has been transformed into a layer of orange rock, granting him superhuman strength and durability<ref name="SDCC2024F4" />
* [[Wyatt Russell]] as [[John Walker (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|John Walker / U.S. Agent]]: A member of the New Avengers who is an enhanced super soldier and a former Captain America<ref name="CastAnnouncementTHR" />
* [[Channing Tatum]] as [[Remy LeBeau (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Remy LeBeau / Gambit]]:<br />A [[Mutant (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|mutant]] capable of charging objects with [[kinetic energy]], causing them to explode upon impact—with [[playing card]]s being his [[Signature weapon|weapon of choice]].<ref name="CastAnnouncementTHR" /> After using a thick, unintelligible [[Cajun accent]] for the character as part of a [[running joke]] in the film ''[[Deadpool & Wolverine]]'' (2024), Tatum said he would not "go full Cajun" in ''Doomsday'', with the Russo brothers wanting the film to have a more dramatic and serious tone.<ref name="TatumSep2025" /> Tatum later clarified that while Gambit would still have a Cajun accent, he would be speaking less [[Cajun French]].<ref name="TatumNov2026" /> Feige said the character in ''Doomsday'' is "fully-rounded" compared to his role in ''Deadpool & Wolverine''.<ref name="FeigeXMenEmpireNov2026" />
* [[Simu Liu]] as [[Xu Shang-Chi]]:<br />An Avenger who wields the mystical [[Ten Rings (object)|Ten Rings]] and is a highly skilled martial artist, trained to be an assassin by his criminal father [[Xu Wenwu]], from whom he inherited the rings.<ref name="CastAnnouncementTHR" /><ref name="LiuEmpireNov2026" /> Liu said Shang-Chi in ''Doomsday'' is older, more self-assured, and "a little more lived in with who he is and his responsibilities" compared to his introduction in the film ''[[Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings]]'' (2021).<ref name="LiuComicBookJan2026" />
* [[Hayley Atwell]] as [[Peggy Carter (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Peggy Carter]]:<br />A 20th-century military agent working for the [[Strategic Scientific Reserve]] (SSR) who is the love interest of Rogers and a founder of [[S.H.I.E.L.D. (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|S.H.I.E.L.D.]]<ref name="SDCC2026Atwell" /> Atwell described the love story between Peggy and Rogers as "a beating heart" to the film.<ref name="EWCoverStoryNov2026" />
* [[Tom Hiddleston]] as [[Loki (Marvel Cinematic Universe)#2012 variant|Loki]]:<br />The Asgardian god of mischief and Thor's adopted brother, based on the Norse mythological deity [[Loki]].<ref name="CastAnnouncementTHR" /> This version of the character was explored in the series ''[[Loki (TV series)|Loki]]'' (2021–2023), where he became the [[God of Stories]] and a guardian of the [[Multiverse (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|multiverse]] at the End of Time.<ref name="HiddlestonEmpireNov2026" /> Hiddleston said that was the starting point for his role in ''Doomsday''.<ref name="HiddlestonTHRJul2026" />
